# DataTable and FinancialTable

> A React financial table: typed rows, render callbacks, a sticky header, controlled sorting, and loading, error and empty states, built on DataTable.

URL: https://design.punji.app/components/data-table/
Section: Data (components)

FinancialTable takes typed rows and render callbacks with a stable row key, semantic row headers, controlled sorting, and loading, error and empty states. DataTable is the lower-level table it is built on. The table never mutates or sorts your data.

## When to use

- Holdings, invoices, transactions and ledgers.
- Controlled sort, search, pagination and selection (with the table hooks).

## When not to use

- Putting business rules in the table: filter and sort in your own state.
- Hiding columns by clipping: they stay reachable through horizontal overflow.

## API

### FinancialTable (component, from @punji/ui/financial)

Holdings, invoices, transactions and ledgers share semantic table behavior, not a business schema.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| caption (required) | `string` |  | Names the table region; also the sort and selection announcements' subject. |
| columns (required) | `readonly FinancialColumn<T>[]` |  | The columns in order: a key, a label, how to render a row's cell, and layout hints (`num`, `wide`, `hideUnder`, `rowHeader`). |
| rows (required) | `readonly T[]` |  | The records to show, in the order to show them. Sort, filter and page them yourself. |
| rowKey (required) | `(row: T) => string` |  | A stable, unique key per row, also the id used by `selection`. |
| state | `"error" \| "loading" \| "ready"` |  | ready (default), loading (a placeholder) or error (`errorTitle`). |
| emptyTitle (required) | `string` |  | The title shown when `rows` is empty (and no search or pagination is on). |
| emptyBody | `ReactNode` |  | A line under the empty title: why it is empty or what to do. |
| emptyAction | `ReactNode` |  | One button or link under the empty state. |
| loadingLabel | `string` |  | Names the loading placeholder. Default "Loading records". |
| errorTitle | `string` |  | What failed, shown in place of the table. Default "Records unavailable". |
| errorAction | `ReactNode` |  | One button for the error state, for example a retry. |
| sort | `{ key: string; dir: SortDir; }` |  | The sort being shown: the column key and its direction. |
| onSort | `((key: string) => void)` |  | Called with the column key a click on a sortable head asks for. The table does not reorder rows. |
| search | `DataTableSearch` |  | Optional controlled search field. The caller filters the complete row set and supplies the filtered page. |
| pagination | `DataTablePagination` |  | Optional controlled page controls. `rowCount` should be the filtered total, including rows on other pages. |
| selection | `DataTableSelection` |  | Optional controlled row selection; selected IDs use `rowKey` and persist across pages in caller state. |
| stack | `boolean` |  | Stack each row into a card on a phone or in a table narrower than 640px (the first column is the card's title, the next its headline figure, the rest are labelled). Default on when the first column is a row header; the sorting heads stay in the accessibility tree. |

### FinancialColumn (type, from @punji/ui/financial)

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| render (required) | `(row: T) => ReactNode` |  | Draws one row's cell for this column. |
| rowHeader | `boolean` |  | The cell is the row's header (a th scope="row"), usually the first column. |
| key (required) | `string` |  | Stable id for the column; the sort key that `onSort` and `sort` use. |
| label (required) | `ReactNode` |  | The column head. |
| num | `boolean` |  | Right-aligned, tabular figures. |
| wide | `boolean` |  | Hidden under 760px. |
| sortable | `boolean` |  | Shows a sort button when `onSort` is given. |
| hideUnder | `1024 \| 1256` |  | Folds away between 760px and this width too (a table with more columns than a tablet column holds). |
| testId | `string` |  | On the head cell. |

### DataTable (component, from @punji/ui/table)

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| caption (required) | `string` |  | Names the table for screen readers: its caption, region and page controls. |
| columns (required) | `Column<K>[]` |  | The columns, in display order. |
| sort | `{ key: K; dir: SortDir; }` |  | The current sort: the sorted column's key and direction. Drives the arrow and aria-sort. |
| onSort | `((key: K) => void)` |  | Called with a column's key when its sort button is pressed. |
| children (required) | `ReactNode` |  | The DataListRow rows. |
| dense | `boolean` |  | A narrow panel's table: no box, tighter cells, row labels that wrap; figures still never wrap. |
| bare | `boolean` |  | No box of its own: the table sits in a Card. |
| stickToPage | `boolean` |  | The head stays in view as the page scrolls (1256px and wider); under that the table scrolls in its own box. |
| stack | `boolean` |  | Under 640px each row is a block: its head and first figure on a line, then four fixed columns, label over value. |
| sortTestIdPrefix | `string` |  | Sort buttons are `${prefix}-${key}`. |
| testId | `string` |  | Test id on the table element. |
| search | `DataTableSearch` |  | Optional controlled search UI. Search the complete data set in the caller, before sorting and pagination. |
| pagination | `DataTablePagination` |  | Optional controlled page controls. `rowCount` is the count after search/filtering. |
| selection | `DataTableSelection` |  | Optional controlled selection. Each selectable DataListRow needs a stable `rowId`. |
| empty | `ReactNode` |  | Content for an empty table. Default: the locale pack's message, else "No records to display." |
| loading | `boolean` |  | Keep headers visible and announce the loading state while the caller fetches rows. |
| loadingLabel | `string` |  | Text announced while `loading` is true. Default: the locale pack's text, else "Loading records…". |
| footer | `ReactNode` |  | A totals row: one DataListRow (its first cell a row header) rendered in a `<tfoot>`, only when there are rows to total. It stacks like a body row on phones. Put your own empty cell first when the table has a selection column. |

## Example: Holdings

Sortable columns, money and price change in cells.

```tsx
import { useMemo, useState } from 'react';
import { FinancialTable, type FinancialColumn } from '@punji/ui/financial';
import { MoneyDisplay } from '@punji/ui/money-display';
import { PriceChange } from '@punji/ui/price-change';
import { nepalMoneyConfig } from '@punji/ui/money';
import { holdings, type Holding } from '../../sample.ts';

const preset = nepalMoneyConfig();
const paisa = (rupees: number) => BigInt(Math.round(rupees * 100));
type Key = 'symbol' | 'qty' | 'ltp' | 'change';

const columns: FinancialColumn<Holding>[] = [
  { key: 'symbol', label: 'Symbol', sortable: true, rowHeader: true, render: (h) => h.symbol },
  { key: 'qty', label: 'Units', num: true, sortable: true, render: (h) => h.qty.toLocaleString('en-IN') },
  { key: 'ltp', label: 'Last price', num: true, sortable: true, render: (h) => <MoneyDisplay value={paisa(h.ltp)} preset={preset} display="none" /> },
  { key: 'change', label: 'Change', num: true, sortable: true, render: (h) => <PriceChange size="sm" preset={preset} showAbsolute={false} current={paisa(h.ltp)} previous={paisa(h.ltp / (1 + h.change / 100))} /> },
];

export default function Example() {
  const [sort, setSort] = useState<{ key: Key; dir: 'asc' | 'desc' }>({ key: 'symbol', dir: 'asc' });
  const rows = useMemo(() => {
    const sign = sort.dir === 'asc' ? 1 : -1;
    return holdings.slice(0, 6).toSorted((a, b) => (a[sort.key] < b[sort.key] ? -sign : a[sort.key] > b[sort.key] ? sign : 0));
  }, [sort]);
  return (
    <div style={{ width: 'min(100%, 720px)', marginInline: 'auto' }}>
    <FinancialTable
      caption="Holdings, prices in NPR"
      columns={columns}
      rows={rows}
      rowKey={(h) => h.symbol}
      sort={sort}
      onSort={(key) => setSort((s) => ({ key: key as Key, dir: s.key === key && s.dir === 'asc' ? 'desc' : 'asc' }))}
      emptyTitle="No holdings yet"
    />
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Example: States

Loading, error and empty are built in.

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { FinancialTable, type FinancialColumn } from '@punji/ui/financial';
import { SegmentedControl } from '@punji/ui/controls';
import { Button } from '@punji/ui/button';
import { holdings, type Holding } from '../../sample.ts';
import { Stack } from '@punji/ui/stack';

const columns: FinancialColumn<Holding>[] = [
  { key: 'symbol', label: 'Symbol', rowHeader: true, render: (h) => h.symbol },
  { key: 'name', label: 'Company', render: (h) => h.name },
];

type View = 'ready' | 'loading' | 'error' | 'empty';

export default function Example() {
  const [view, setView] = useState<View>('loading');
  return (
    <Stack>
      <SegmentedControl<View>
        label="State"
        prefix="table-state"
        size="sm"
        value={view}
        onChange={setView}
        options={[{ value: 'ready', label: 'Ready' }, { value: 'loading', label: 'Loading' }, { value: 'error', label: 'Error' }, { value: 'empty', label: 'Empty' }]}
      />
      <FinancialTable
        caption="Holdings"
        columns={columns}
        rows={view === 'ready' ? holdings.slice(0, 3) : []}
        rowKey={(h) => h.symbol}
        state={view === 'loading' || view === 'error' ? view : 'ready'}
        emptyTitle="No holdings yet"
        emptyBody="Add a holding to see it here."
        errorAction={<Button size="sm" variant="secondary" onClick={() => setView('loading')}>Try again</Button>}
      />
    </Stack>
  );
}
```

## Example: Search and pages

Controlled search and pagination with usePagination.

```tsx
import { useMemo, useState } from 'react';
import { FinancialTable, type FinancialColumn } from '@punji/ui/financial';
import { usePagination } from '@punji/ui/hooks';
import { holdings, type Holding } from '../../sample.ts';

const columns: FinancialColumn<Holding>[] = [
  { key: 'symbol', label: 'Symbol', rowHeader: true, render: (h) => h.symbol },
  { key: 'name', label: 'Company', render: (h) => h.name },
  { key: 'qty', label: 'Units', num: true, render: (h) => h.qty },
];

export default function Example() {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('');
  const filtered = useMemo(() => holdings.filter((h) => `${h.symbol} ${h.name}`.toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase())), [query]);
  const pager = usePagination({ total: filtered.length, defaultPageSize: 4 });
  return (
    <FinancialTable
      caption="Holdings"
      columns={columns}
      rows={filtered.slice(pager.startIndex, pager.endIndex)}
      rowKey={(h) => h.symbol}
      emptyTitle="No holdings match"
      search={{ label: 'Search holdings', value: query, onChange: (value) => { setQuery(value); pager.setPage(1); }, placeholder: 'Symbol or company' }}
      pagination={{ pageIndex: pager.pageIndex, pageSize: pager.pageSize, rowCount: filtered.length, onPageChange: (index) => pager.setPage(index + 1) }}
    />
  );
}
```

## Keyboard behaviour

- Sort headers are buttons: Tab to one, Enter or Space to sort.
- Search, pagination and selection controls are native controls in tab order.

## Accessibility

- A real <table> with a caption, scoped headers and `aria-sort` on the sorted column.
- The first column can be a row header for screen-reader navigation.
- Loading is announced with a status label; errors with `role="alert"`.

## Responsive behaviour

- Wide tables scroll horizontally inside their container; columns can fold away under set widths (`hideUnder`).


