# StockTable

> A React stock table for NEPSE or any market: symbol, LTP, change, volume, turnover and a trend line. You own the data and sort; prices are exact bigint.

URL: https://design.punji.app/components/stock-table/
Section: Stock market (components)

A full quote board: symbol over name, LTP, change, volume, turnover and an optional trend line, built on DataTable. The caller owns the data and the sort (sortQuotes plus controlled props); nothing here fetches, filters or re-sorts. Prices are exact bigint minor units, and a missing value is a dash with a spoken "No value", never zero.

## When to use

- A whole market or sector board where people sort and compare.
- Row selection and column choice (with `useColumnVisibility`).
- Live prices fed from your own socket or query, with `live` to count and flash each new LTP.

## When not to use

- A short top-N list: use `MarketMovers`. The stocks a person follows: use Watchlist. Arbitrary records: use `FinancialTable`.
- Search and pagination: they are not built in. Filter first, sort the matches, then slice.
- Passing floating-point prices: the types require bigint minor units.

## API

### StockTable (component, from @punji/ui/stock-table)

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| caption (required) | `string` |  | Names the table region; also the sort and selection announcements' subject. |
| quotes (required) | `readonly T[]` |  | Rows in the order to show. Sort them yourself (`sortQuotes`). Keys are `symbol`, so values can update in place. |
| columns | `readonly StockColumn[]` |  | Columns to show, in order. Default symbol, LTP, change, volume, turnover. `symbol` is always shown. Feed it from `useColumnVisibility().visible`. |
| labels | `Partial<Record<StockColumn, string>>` |  | Overrides for the column heads, in the reader's language. |
| sort | `QuoteSort` |  | The sort being shown. Heads are sort buttons only when `onSortChange` is given. |
| onSortChange | `((sort: QuoteSort) => void)` |  | Called with the sort a click on a column head asks for: a new column starts ascending for the symbol and descending for figures, and a repeat click on the sorted column flips its direction (the rule `nextQuoteSort` implements). The table does not reorder rows: sort `quotes` yourself and pass `sort` back. |
| money | `MoneyFormatConfig` |  | Currency and locale of prices and turnover. Default NPR, en-IN, no currency mark. |
| convention | `"green-up" \| "red-up"` |  | Per-instance override of which hue means up: 'green-up' or 'red-up' (absolute, never a second swap on top of the theme). Default: follow the theme's gain and loss colours (`createTheme({ finance })`), which is the one place to set the convention. |
| changeLabels | `PriceChangeLabels` |  | Spoken direction words for the change. |
| selectedSymbols | `readonly string[]` |  | Selected symbols (controlled). Give `onSelectedSymbolsChange` to show checkboxes. |
| onSelectedSymbolsChange | `((symbols: readonly string[]) => void)` |  | Called with the new list of selected symbols when a row checkbox changes. Keep it in state and pass it back as `selectedSymbols`. |
| selectLabel | `((symbol: string) => string)` |  | Accessible name of a row checkbox. Default `Select NABIL`. |
| density | `"comfortable" \| "compact"` |  | comfortable (default) or compact rows. |
| bare | `boolean` |  | No box of its own: the table sits in a card or a panel. |
| maxHeight | `string \| number` |  | The head sticks inside a box this tall that scrolls ('420px', 420). Without it the table is as tall as its rows. |
| stickToPage | `boolean` |  | The head sticks to the page as it scrolls (wide screens). |
| stack | `boolean` |  | Rows become blocks under 640 px (default true). |
| live | `boolean` |  | The LTP counts to each new value and flashes its direction (needs live data; honours reduced motion). |
| renderSymbol | `((quote: T) => ReactNode)` |  | What the symbol cell holds, for example a link to the stock page. Default the symbol over the name. |
| state | `"error" \| "loading" \| "ready"` |  | ready (default), loading (headers stay, rows replaced by a status line) or error. |
| emptyLabel | `ReactNode` |  | Shown in place of rows when `quotes` is empty and `state` is `ready`. Default 'No quotes to show.' |
| loadingLabel | `string` |  | The status line shown while `state` is `loading`. Default 'Loading quotes…'. |
| errorLabel | `ReactNode` |  | What failed, shown with the retry button when `state` is `error`. Default 'Quotes could not be loaded.' |
| retryLabel | `string` |  | The retry button's words when `state` is `error`. Default 'Try again'. |
| onRetry | `(() => void)` |  | Called when the retry button is pressed. The error line shows the button only when this is given, so give it whenever `state` can be `error` and a retry is possible. |
| testId | `string` |  | Sets `data-testid` on the root; inner parts get derived ids (`<id>-head-<column>`, `<id>-row-<symbol>`). |

### Quote (type, from @punji/ui/stock-table)

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| symbol (required) | `string` |  | Unique, stable key (the ticker). |
| name | `string` |  | The company's name, printed under the symbol in the default symbol cell. |
| sector | `string` |  | The company's sector, for your own grouping and filtering. The display components here do not print it. |
| ltp (required) | `bigint \| null` |  | Last traded price, minor units. |
| previousClose (required) | `bigint \| null` |  | Previous close, minor units; the base of the change. |
| volume (required) | `number \| null` |  | Shares traded. |
| turnover (required) | `bigint \| null` |  | Value traded, minor units. |
| history | `readonly (number \| null)[]` |  | Closes for a trend line, oldest first. |
| lowerLimit | `bigint \| null` |  | Daily circuit limits, minor units, when the exchange publishes them. |
| upperLimit | `bigint \| null` |  | The upper daily circuit limit, minor units, when the exchange publishes it (see `lowerLimit`). Pass it to `PriceLimitIndicator`; the tables do not print it. |

### sortQuotes (function, from @punji/ui/stock-table)

A new array ordered by `sort`. Stable (equal values keep their input order,
in both directions) and null-last in both directions, so it is a total
order: the same input always gives the same output. Symbols compare by
upper-cased code units, not by the reader's locale. The input is never
mutated.

```ts
function sortQuotes: <T extends Quote>(quotes: readonly T[], sort: QuoteSort) => T[]
```

### nextQuoteSort (function, from @punji/ui/stock-table)

What a click on a column head asks for: the symbol starts ascending, figures start with the largest. A second click on the same column flips it.

```ts
function nextQuoteSort: (current: QuoteSort | undefined, key: QuoteSortKey) => QuoteSort
```

### quoteChange (function, from @punji/ui/stock-table)

Absolute change in minor units, or null when either price is missing.

```ts
function quoteChange: (quote: Pick<Quote, "ltp" | "previousClose">) => bigint | null
```

### quoteChangePercent (function, from @punji/ui/stock-table)

Change in percent, or null (missing price, or a previous close that is not positive).

```ts
function quoteChangePercent: (quote: Pick<Quote, "ltp" | "previousClose">) => number | null
```

## Example: Sortable board

Click a column to sort. The head stays put while the board scrolls.

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { StockTable, sortQuotes, type QuoteSort, type StockColumn } from '@punji/ui/stock-table';
import { useColumnVisibility } from '@punji/ui/use-column-visibility';
import { quotes } from '../../sample.ts';

const ALL: StockColumn[] = ['symbol', 'ltp', 'change', 'volume', 'turnover', 'trend'];

export default function Example() {
  const [sort, setSort] = useState<QuoteSort>({ key: 'changePercent', dir: 'desc' });
  const columns = useColumnVisibility({ columns: ALL, defaultHidden: new Set(['trend']) });
  return (
    <StockTable
      caption="NEPSE quotes, NPR"
      quotes={sortQuotes(quotes, sort)}
      sort={sort}
      onSortChange={setSort}
      columns={columns.visible as StockColumn[]}
      maxHeight={360}
    />
  );
}
```

